From 2bb339d8929b488ba010fcad2944edbf647cdbb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:31:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] usb: typec: ucsi: run connector change handling on the
 freezable workqueue

The same unplug-during-s2idle also raises a UCSI connector change, and
ucsi_handle_connector_change() runs on system_wq while devices are
suspended. On pmic_glink it sets the orientation through the FSA4480
switch over a suspended I2C bus:

  i2c i2c-2: Transfer while suspended
  Workqueue: events ucsi_handle_connector_change
   fsa4480_set / typec_switch_set / typec_set_orientation
   pmic_glink_ucsi_connector_status / ucsi_handle_connector_change

and the board again never comes back from s2idle. Queue the work on
system_freezable_wq; EVENT_PENDING already folds events that arrive
before it runs, so the change is handled once after resume. With this
and the altmode change, unplugging the sink during suspend and pressing
the power key resumes normally.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index bef3f9b71..b9126d71d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1575,7 +1575,7 @@ void ucsi_connector_change(struct ucsi *ucsi, u8 num)
 	con = &ucsi->connector[num - 1];
 
 	if (!test_and_set_bit(EVENT_PENDING, &ucsi->flags))
-		schedule_work(&con->work);
+		queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &con->work);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ucsi_connector_change);
 
